01:14:18.390 --> 01:14:22.260
The confident grades are, I think,

01:14:22.260 --> 01:14:29.320
interesting in problems in which the distribution of beliefs is typically by model.

01:14:29.740 --> 01:14:32.120
We've shown, actually,

01:14:32.120 --> 01:14:37.080
in a specific paper that how people build

01:14:37.080 --> 01:14:39.750
confidence on these problems and how people build

01:14:39.750 --> 01:14:44.025
confidence on perceptual problems like pointing to [inaudible] stock,

01:14:44.025 --> 01:14:46.500
leads to very different distributions,

01:14:46.500 --> 01:14:50.805
which leads to very different ways in which confidence is being constructed.

01:14:50.805 --> 01:14:55.020
Essentially, the main difference it has to do with

01:14:55.020 --> 01:14:59.805
the idea from what's the universe from which they sample data.

01:14:59.805 --> 01:15:03.285
Typically, in polarized problems,

01:15:03.285 --> 01:15:06.435
it is as if this is a model,

01:15:06.435 --> 01:15:08.700
this is a very simplified model so

01:15:08.700 --> 01:15:11.220
that I'm not speaking exactly how it works in our brain,

01:15:11.220 --> 01:15:18.940
but a model in which you let people sample from two different distributions, arguments.

01:15:19.580 --> 01:15:22.440
Imagine the genetic problem I gave,

01:15:22.440 --> 01:15:24.945
so the arguments in favor would be,

01:15:24.945 --> 01:15:29.010
we try to make the best for our children and we use the arguments we have,

01:15:29.010 --> 01:15:30.720
we use education, why not use genetics?

01:15:30.720 --> 01:15:32.700
I'm not saying this is right, I'm saying this is an argument.

01:15:32.700 --> 01:15:35.565
An argument against would be like,

01:15:35.565 --> 01:15:42.060
this will lead to Aryan like the typical genic nightmare.

01:15:42.060 --> 01:15:47.175
We will all converge to monochromatic humans.

01:15:47.175 --> 01:15:49.980
What I'm trying to say is that those arguments,

01:15:49.980 --> 01:15:51.135
you see, they're very discreet,

01:15:51.135 --> 01:15:52.320
and I could pick many more,

01:15:52.320 --> 01:15:55.020
but they seem to be picked from their very different bats.

01:15:55.020 --> 01:15:57.255
It builds up all this vision,

01:15:57.255 --> 01:15:59.250
in which you may have a number of arguments from

01:15:59.250 --> 01:16:01.380
this bag and a number of words from this bag,

01:16:01.380 --> 01:16:03.540
and then people that are the high confident grades are

01:16:03.540 --> 01:16:05.700
the one that actually sample from both of them,

01:16:05.700 --> 01:16:07.950
and the ones that are below confident grades are

01:16:07.950 --> 01:16:10.500
the ones that actually have very low sampling,

01:16:10.500 --> 01:16:12.780
so essentially they don't understand the problem and they think it's

01:16:12.780 --> 01:16:15.930
just too complicated and they then don't want to think about it.

01:16:15.930 --> 01:16:18.630
It's a very different perspective.

01:16:18.630 --> 01:16:24.810
I don't think the high confident grade argument would work for unimodal distributions.

01:16:24.810 --> 01:16:26.610
Like in the problem,

01:16:26.610 --> 01:16:28.185
I forgot the name,

01:16:28.185 --> 01:16:29.700
he or she mentioned,

01:16:29.700 --> 01:16:31.020
like the bloody pointing to [inaudible]

01:16:31.020 --> 01:16:33.810
stock problems that are typically perceptual problems.

01:16:33.810 --> 01:16:37.080
This has not been shown and I don't think it would work there,

01:16:37.080 --> 01:16:39.250
I think the intuition is right.

01:16:40.010 --> 01:16:43.800
I think we have a good reason to understand why it would not work,

01:16:43.800 --> 01:16:48.750
which again its confidence is constructed very differently in these problems.

