It's been known for years that people like,

01:17:20.595 --> 01:17:22.830
and actually we just have a paper on this,

01:17:22.830 --> 01:17:27.190
people like other people that think like them.

01:17:27.980 --> 01:17:31.245
This is very universal, it's very conserved.

01:17:31.245 --> 01:17:34.020
Of course, you should not take this argument as you

01:17:34.020 --> 01:17:36.795
will not like someone that thinks differently from you.

01:17:36.795 --> 01:17:41.430
It's a statistical argument that we tend to like more,

01:17:41.430 --> 01:17:44.295
we tend to prefer, and we tend to have many, many more friends.

01:17:44.295 --> 01:17:47.745
Actually, each of you in the audience can do the experiment.

01:17:47.745 --> 01:17:51.300
How many people around you do you have that think

01:17:51.300 --> 01:17:55.590
radically different from you like in first question, second question?

01:17:55.590 --> 01:18:01.110
Take 15 different problems like taxes,

01:18:01.110 --> 01:18:05.805
abortion, drugs, foreign policy.

01:18:05.805 --> 01:18:09.810
Take a number of them and think how you think about all of them.

01:18:09.810 --> 01:18:13.230
Think how the majority of the people think about these people.

01:18:13.230 --> 01:18:15.510
If you're like the majority of people,

01:18:15.510 --> 01:18:17.625
you'll find a very strong correlation.

01:18:17.625 --> 01:18:23.020
You do agree on a lot of problems that when you think about them,

01:18:23.020 --> 01:18:25.265
they are really independent problems.

01:18:25.265 --> 01:18:27.860
Me being liberal on this does not imply that I

01:18:27.860 --> 01:18:30.635
have to be liberal on this and I can be conservative of this other.

01:18:30.635 --> 01:18:33.640
But we tend to be very partisan.

01:18:33.640 --> 01:18:36.735
I say we tend is a statistical finding

01:18:36.735 --> 01:18:39.690
that the vast majority of the people are like this.

01:18:39.690 --> 01:18:42.465
Interestingly, those are experiments done in sociology.

01:18:42.465 --> 01:18:44.220
The more educated the people they are,

01:18:44.220 --> 01:18:45.600
the more correlated they are.

01:18:45.600 --> 01:18:50.430
If you take in the US the axes of what Democrats think about a particular problem,

01:18:50.430 --> 01:18:54.840
what's a typical Democrat reaction to any particular problem?

01:18:54.840 --> 01:18:56.880
What's the typical Republican?

01:18:56.880 --> 01:18:58.680
This is 20 years ago,

01:18:58.680 --> 01:19:01.320
now Republican, it's spreads in axis.

01:19:01.320 --> 01:19:06.960
But typically when really there was a two-dimensional layout of political spread,

01:19:06.960 --> 01:19:08.805
the most of the violence in the US.

01:19:08.805 --> 01:19:12.960
Then you spread people in these domains, and you ask,

01:19:12.960 --> 01:19:14.340
how much people look alike,

01:19:14.340 --> 01:19:15.765
how correlated they are,

01:19:15.765 --> 01:19:18.450
and you measure this as a function of education.

01:19:18.450 --> 01:19:21.030
The more educated people they are,

01:19:21.030 --> 01:19:22.140
the more correlated they are,

01:19:22.140 --> 01:19:27.330
the more they begin to think alike because they form these tribes in which why is this?

01:19:27.330 --> 01:19:31.350
This is a response to your question because they're intelligent people.

01:19:31.350 --> 01:19:34.245
I speak in third person, but I make all these emirs,

01:19:34.245 --> 01:19:36.330
I'm not excluded from any of these.

01:19:36.330 --> 01:19:41.925
But we tend to listen arguments that

01:19:41.925 --> 01:19:48.585
we unconsciously gather to confirm our beliefs because this is very comfortable.

01:19:48.585 --> 01:19:50.655
How this happens,

01:19:50.655 --> 01:19:53.400
we did one study which I think at least to me it was

01:19:53.400 --> 01:19:55.935
very enlightening on the complexity of this problem.

01:19:55.935 --> 01:19:58.410
Because this is true, of course,

01:19:58.410 --> 01:20:00.210
this is worse in social networks because

01:20:00.210 --> 01:20:02.550
people in social networks follow who they want to follow,

01:20:02.550 --> 01:20:06.480
and so they get a lot of evidence that confirms what they want to do, which is true.

01:20:06.480 --> 01:20:08.400
Take vaccines.

01:20:08.400 --> 01:20:09.960
I'm vaccinated,

01:20:09.960 --> 01:20:11.430
I'm completely in favor of vaccines.

01:20:11.430 --> 01:20:13.290
Here I'm going to say my [inaudible], it's not important,

01:20:13.290 --> 01:20:16.230
but if there's information,

01:20:16.230 --> 01:20:19.995
some information that shows that vaccines do cover risk.

01:20:19.995 --> 01:20:23.895
The obvious fact for this is that, for instance,

01:20:23.895 --> 01:20:26.115
I'm sure I want to vaccinate myself,

01:20:26.115 --> 01:20:30.105
I do not think I would like to vaccinate a six month old baby.

01:20:30.105 --> 01:20:36.615
This is just a recognition that I understand that there are arguments against it.

01:20:36.615 --> 01:20:41.775
In my opinion, the arguments in favor are much more sound and hence I make my conclusion.

01:20:41.775 --> 01:20:45.330
But if I only were to look at these arguments,

01:20:45.330 --> 01:20:47.040
and this is, once again,

01:20:47.040 --> 01:20:48.570
the only space I'm looking for,

01:20:48.570 --> 01:20:54.630
I will rationally make a conclusion that this is the wrong thing to do because I

01:20:54.630 --> 01:20:57.630
do have papers and evidence that show all what I want to

01:20:57.630 --> 01:21:01.215
see that proves that I have to stand where I do stand.

01:21:01.215 --> 01:21:03.210
How does this work in social networks?

01:21:03.210 --> 01:21:06.585
There are fact-checking companies that

01:21:06.585 --> 01:21:10.680
understood this problem and so they said we need to provide balanced evidence.

01:21:10.680 --> 01:21:14.640
We need to provide evidence showing that the good people do good things,

01:21:14.640 --> 01:21:15.750
the good people do bad things,

01:21:15.750 --> 01:21:17.760
the bad people do good things and the bad people do good things,

01:21:17.760 --> 01:21:19.875
so that people understand that reality is more complex.

01:21:19.875 --> 01:21:21.705
Perfect. Now, what happens?

01:21:21.705 --> 01:21:24.375
You can see this as a distribution of evidence,

01:21:24.375 --> 01:21:27.765
so against the favor or against the divide mobile evidence, I would say.

01:21:27.765 --> 01:21:29.220
You can think about vaccines.

01:21:29.220 --> 01:21:30.660
You should vaccinate because of these,

01:21:30.660 --> 01:21:33.180
but you should worry because of this, you should do it because of this,

01:21:33.180 --> 01:21:34.650
but beware with that,

01:21:34.650 --> 01:21:37.590
and it's providing all the evidence. Now, what is the problem?

01:21:37.590 --> 01:21:42.015
The problem is that these companies have like say, one million followers.

01:21:42.015 --> 01:21:46.515
But then the followers of these companies retweet

01:21:46.515 --> 01:21:51.315
or re-share the information that they get to 50 million people.

01:21:51.315 --> 01:21:55.440
This 50 million people do not receive directly from the fact-checking company,

01:21:55.440 --> 01:21:57.615
they receive it from who they want to receive it.

01:21:57.615 --> 01:21:59.370
It's like a rectifier.

01:21:59.370 --> 01:22:02.954
This company is showing balanced information,

01:22:02.954 --> 01:22:05.340
but then there are social rectifiers that

01:22:05.340 --> 01:22:08.280
fill the information and only let this one pass,

01:22:08.280 --> 01:22:10.440
and there are people that are downstream from

01:22:10.440 --> 01:22:12.495
this rectifiers because they have this belief,

01:22:12.495 --> 01:22:14.265
they have the belief that vaccines are wrong,

01:22:14.265 --> 01:22:17.595
so they only follow people that provide information that consume this vaccine,

01:22:17.595 --> 01:22:19.680
and they get more and more convinced.

01:22:19.680 --> 01:22:21.645
Once again, I want to make the claim,

01:22:21.645 --> 01:22:23.775
it's not like they are thinking wrong,

01:22:23.775 --> 01:22:27.645
they are thinking on the wrong subset of the data.

01:22:27.645 --> 01:22:32.685
This is wrong, but restricted to this particular constraint,

01:22:32.685 --> 01:22:35.535
the conclusions that they often make are right,

01:22:35.535 --> 01:22:39.285
are the right conclusions from just looking at a small subset of the data.

01:22:39.285 --> 01:22:43.285
This is a very clear example of how, once you have a belief,

01:22:43.285 --> 01:22:48.515
you decide to sample data on a way that only confirms the beliefs that you had,

01:22:48.515 --> 01:22:50.810
and you gather real data that actually will

01:22:50.810 --> 01:22:53.650
prove more and more that you are right to think that.

01:22:53.650 --> 01:22:57.000
Even when you have a broader set of data available,

01:22:57.000 --> 01:23:00.330
you gravitate towards the bits of data.

01:23:00.330 --> 01:23:01.950
Yeah. This is also very typical.

01:23:01.950 --> 01:23:05.140
Even exactly, this is very important to what you're saying.

01:23:09.850 --> 01:23:12.590
We tend to think this as irrationality,

01:23:12.590 --> 01:23:14.270
but this is in the essence of science.

01:23:14.270 --> 01:23:17.525
When we make the typical scientific claim

01:23:17.525 --> 01:23:22.350
of great claims imply or require great evidence,

01:23:22.350 --> 01:23:25.620
like if I want to say that the speed of light is not constant,

01:23:25.620 --> 01:23:27.945
then I really should have a lot of evidence.

01:23:27.945 --> 01:23:31.305
Why? Because we have a strong belief, a strong prior,

01:23:31.305 --> 01:23:33.135
if you think this as Bayesian thinking,

01:23:33.135 --> 01:23:36.600
like I do have a lot of aggregated knowledge that tells me.

01:23:36.600 --> 01:23:39.030
So if I do have information of

01:23:39.030 --> 01:23:41.100
the same value in favor of what I

01:23:41.100 --> 01:23:43.830
have a strong prior and against what I have a strong prior,

01:23:43.830 --> 01:23:46.470
Priya as you were saying, I would not weigh them in the same manner.

01:23:46.470 --> 01:23:48.900
This is exactly what you'd expect from

01:23:48.900 --> 01:23:52.360
a rational Bayesian thinker, this is the thing they do.

